---

<Layout
  title="Nemesysco UI/UX design project by Valeri Ciutac"
  className="dark:bg-[#00132F] bg-[#B9CEEE]"
>
  <ProjectHeader
    projectName="Nemesysco"
    projectStack="Figma, JavaScript, After Effects"
    projectFocus="Adjusting UX and Optimizing App Design"
    projectImage="../../projects/nemesysco/Nemesysco-header.webp"
    projectDescription="Nemesysco's app is a unique blend of technology and implementation. The app design needed to be simple and present a ton of information in real time, all while focusing the viewer on the important parts of the app.The challenge was to come up with a progressive disclosure of information and emphasizing different parts of the app at varying intervals."
  />

  <!-- <ContentWithMedia
    imageFirst={false}
    backgroundColor="#ececec"
    imageCellWidth={6}
    contentCellWidth={6}
    contentImage="../../projects/nemesysco/EmotionLogic-diamond.png"
    contentTitle="What is The Emotional Diamond?"
    contentDescription="Nemesysco’s Emotional Diamond, developed in 2012, simplifies the visualization of complex emotional responses detected by the LVA. It consists of 8 key indicators: Energy, Stress, Logic & Confidence, Emotion, Passion, Uneasy, Mental Effort, and Concentration (out of 14 total emotional states). The core idea is that emotions are context-dependent, not inherently good or bad. By analyzing emotional patterns over time, the Emotional Diamond helps reveal deeper personality traits and reactions."
  /> -->

  <Heading
    title="The Problem"
    subtitle="Nemesysco required a desktop interface for their deep-tech voice and emotion analysis software. While the underlying machine learning engine analyzed only audio data, the interface needed to display a synchronized video feed alongside the real-time emotional telemetry. The primary UX challenges were twofold: managing severe cognitive load (ensuring analysts could monitor the subject without missing data updates) and enabling efficient retrospective review (allowing researchers to quickly find critical moments in hours of footage)."
  />

  <VideoEmbedWithContent
    imageCellOrder={1}
    contentCellOrder={2}
    contentOrder={1}
    imageCellWidth={6}
    contentCellWidth={6}
    videoLink=`https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ux33qb-UUyE?si=GI5cn1vyr3D4_u55 width="560" height="315"
    allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen
    `
    contentTitle="Barebones UI was lacking features"
    contentDescription="The old interface lacked essential shortcuts to key timeline milestones and offered no immediate, real-time synthesis of the subject's emotional state, causing user fatigue."
  />

  <Heading title="The Process" subtitle="" />

  <div class="max-w-7xl py-20 mx-auto px-6">
    <div class="mb-16">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[--text]">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
            <div
              class="w-10 h-10 flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#F68C24]/20 text-[#F68C24] font-bold text-lg"
            >
              2
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[--text]">
              Spatial Architecture (The Split-Attention Problem)
            </h3>
          </div>
        </h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[--text-sub] max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Managing user expectations before and during AI output by establishing
        clear temporal states. I designed a clear visual progression to dictate
        exactly what the user sees from standby to full synthesis.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-12 relative items-start">
      <div
        class="w-full md:w-1/2 sticky top-24 bg-[#243E64] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg h-[250px] md:h-[380px] z-10 flex items-center justify-center"
      >
        <div
          data-visual="1"
          class="visual-frame absolute inset-0 transition-all duration-700 ease-in-out flex items-center justify-center p-8 md:p-12"
          style="opacity: 1; transform: scale(1);"
        >
          <img
            src="../../projects/nemesysco/standby.webp"
            alt="Standby State"
            class="max-w-full max-h-full object-contain drop-shadow-md"
          />
        </div>

        <div
          data-visual="2"
          class="visual-frame absolute inset-0 transition-all duration-700 ease-in-out flex items-center justify-center p-8 md:p-12 pointer-events-none"
          style="opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.95);"
        >
          <img
            src="../../projects/nemesysco/active.webp"
            alt="Active State"
            class="max-w-full max-h-full object-contain drop-shadow-md"
          />
        </div>

        <div
          data-visual="3"
          class="visual-frame absolute inset-0 transition-all duration-700 ease-in-out flex items-center justify-center p-8 md:p-12 pointer-events-none"
          style="opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.95);"
        >
          <img
            src="../../projects/nemesysco/synthesis.webp"
            alt="Synthesis State"
            class="max-w-full max-h-full object-contain drop-shadow-md"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="w-full md:w-1/2 pt-8 md:pt-[10vh] pb-[20vh] md:pb-[30vh]">
        <div
          data-target="1"
          class="scroll-step cursor-pointer transition-all duration-500 py-12 md:py-16 mb-12 md:mb-24 border-l-4 pl-8"
          style="opacity: 1; border-color: #F68C24;"
        >
          <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[--text] mb-4">
            Phase 1: Standby
          </h4>
          <p class="text-[--text-sub] leading-relaxed text-lg">
            The UI displays the core diamond framework using dashed lines. This
            establishes the spatial footprint of the visualization and indicates
            system readiness, even before any audio data is processed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          data-target="2"
          class="scroll-step cursor-pointer transition-all duration-500 py-12 md:py-16 mb-12 md:mb-24 border-l-4 pl-8"
          style="opacity: 0.3; border-color: transparent;"
        >
          <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[--text] mb-4">
            Phase 2: Active Analysis
          </h4>
          <p class="text-[--text-sub] leading-relaxed text-lg">
            Once audio input is detected, the radar animates in real-time. By
            keeping the UI otherwise "quiet," the user's attention is drawn
            exclusively to the live geometry shifts of the emotion mapping.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          data-target="3"
          class="scroll-step cursor-pointer transition-all duration-500 py-12 md:py-16 border-l-4 pl-8"
          style="opacity: 0.3; border-color: transparent;"
        >
          <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[--text] mb-4">
            Phase 3: Contextual Synthesis
          </h4>
          <p class="text-[--text-sub] leading-relaxed text-lg">
            The macro "Current Emotional Style" text is purposefully delayed. It
            renders only after the system has processed enough data to establish
            a reliable baseline, preventing erratic or confusing initial
            readings.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
      const steps = document.querySelectorAll(".scroll-step");
      const visuals = document.querySelectorAll(".visual-frame");

      const activateStep = (targetIndex) => {
        if (!targetIndex) return;

        // 1. Update text styles
        steps.forEach((step) => {
          if (step.getAttribute("data-target") === targetIndex) {
            step.style.opacity = "1";
            step.style.borderColor = "#F68C24";
          } else {
            step.style.opacity = "0.3";
            step.style.borderColor = "transparent";
          }
        });

        // 2. Update image styles (Pure crossfade, no z-index popping)
        visuals.forEach((visual) => {
          if (visual.getAttribute("data-visual") === targetIndex) {
            visual.style.opacity = "1";
            visual.style.transform = "scale(1)";
          } else {
            visual.style.opacity = "0";
            visual.style.transform = "scale(0.95)";
          }
        });
      };

      // Keep track of which elements are currently intersecting the view
      const visibleTargets = new Set();

      const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries) => {
          entries.forEach((entry) => {
            const target = entry.target.getAttribute("data-target");

            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              visibleTargets.add(target);
            } else {
              visibleTargets.delete(target);
            }
          });

          // If multiple items are in view, always prioritize the one highest on the page (lowest number)
          if (visibleTargets.size > 0) {
            const activeTarget = Math.min(
              ...Array.from(visibleTargets).map(Number),
            ).toString();
            activateStep(activeTarget);
          }
        },
        {
          // Creates a wide 40% trigger zone in the center of the screen
          rootMargin: "-30% 0px -30% 0px",
          threshold: 0,
        },
      );

      steps.forEach((step) => observer.observe(step));

      // Handle clicks
      steps.forEach((step) => {
        step.addEventListener("click", function () {
          this.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "center" });
        });
      });
    });
  </script>

  <div class="max-w-7xl py-20 mx-auto px-6">
    <!-- Section Intro -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
        <div
          class="w-10 h-10 flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#F68C24]/20 text-[#F68C24] font-bold text-lg"
        >
          2
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[--text]">
          Spatial Architecture (The Split-Attention Problem)
        </h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[--text-sub] max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        The original system utilized a "Picture-in-Picture" overlay for the LVA
        data. I analyzed the physical viewing habits of analysts and discovered
        this layout caused severe cognitive fatigue. I mapped the eye travel
        (saccades) to prove that a strict side-by-side layout was mathematically
        required to prevent missed facial micro-expressions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Interactive Toggle Component -->
    <div
      class="bg-[#243E64] rounded-2xl border border-white/5 p-4 md:p-10 shadow-lg"
    >
      <!-- Controls (The Toggle Switch) -->
      <div
        class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-start md:items-center mb-8 md:mb-10 gap-6"
      >
        <div>
          <h4
            id="architecture-title"
            class="text-xl font-bold text-[--text] mb-2 transition-colors"
          >
            The Problem: Floating Overlays
          </h4>
          <p
            id="architecture-desc"
            class="text-[--text-sub] max-w-lg text-sm md:text-base"
          >
            Forces complex diagonal eye travel and creates visual interference.
            The moving video behind the chart creates a constant figure-ground
            conflict for the brain.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Toggle Buttons -->
        <div
          class="flex bg-slate-900/50 p-1 rounded-lg border border-white/10 shrink-0 w-full md:w-auto"
        >
          <button
            data-toggle="problem"
            class="arch-btn active relative flex-1 md:flex-none px-4 md:px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md text-xs md:text-sm font-semibold text-white bg-[#F68C24] shadow-md transition-all"
          >
            Original Overlay
          </button>
          <button
            data-toggle="solution"
            class="arch-btn relative flex-1 md:flex-none px-4 md:px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md text-xs md:text-sm font-semibold text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-all"
          >
            My Architecture
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Visualization Canvas -->
      <div
        class="relative w-full h-[300px] md:h-[450px] bg-slate-900/80 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-white/5"
      >
        <!-- STATE 1: THE PROBLEM (Diagonal Overlay) -->
        <div
          id="view-problem"
          class="absolute inset-0 transition-opacity duration-500 opacity-100 flex items-center justify-center p-4 md:p-8"
        >
          <!-- Mock Video Feed (Full container) -->
          <div
            class="w-full h-full max-w-3xl bg-slate-800 rounded-lg border border-slate-700 flex items-center justify-center relative overflow-hidden"
          >
            <span
              class="text-slate-500 font-mono text-sm md:text-lg tracking-widest opacity-50"
              >VIDEO FEED</span
            >

            <!-- Mock Floating Overlay (Top Right) -->
            <div
              class="absolute top-4 right-4 md:top-8 md:right-8 w-24 h-24 md:w-48 md:h-48 bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-600 rounded-lg shadow-2xl flex items-center justify-center backdrop-blur-md z-10"
            >
              <span
                class="text-slate-400 font-mono text-[10px] md:text-sm text-center px-2"
                >LVA OVERLAY</span
              >
            </div>

            <!-- Diagonal Saccade Warning Line -->
            <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full pointer-events-none z-0">
              <line
                x1="50%"
                y1="50%"
                x2="85%"
                y2="15%"
                stroke="rgba(239,68,68,0.4)"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-dasharray="6"></line>
            </svg>

            <!-- Warning Tag -->
            <div
              class="absolute top-1/2 left-[10%] md:left-1/4 -translate-y-1/2 bg-red-500/10 border border-red-500/30 text-red-400 px-3 py-1.5 md:px-4 md:py-2 rounded text-[10px] md:text-xs font-mono text-center z-10"
            >
              DIAGONAL FATIGUE
            </div>

            <!-- Eye Tracking Node -->
            <div
              class="eye-tracker-diagonal absolute w-3 h-3 md:w-4 md:h-4 bg-red-500 rounded-full shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(239,68,68,0.8)] z-20"
            >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STATE 2: THE SOLUTION (Horizontal Side-by-Side Locked) -->
        <div
          id="view-solution"
          class="absolute inset-0 transition-opacity duration-500 opacity-0 pointer-events-none flex flex-row items-center justify-center p-4 md:p-8 gap-2 md:gap-8"
        >
          <!-- Mock Video Feed -->
          <div
            class="w-1/2 h-40 md:h-full md:max-h-[300px] bg-slate-800 rounded-lg border border-slate-700 flex items-center justify-center relative"
          >
            <span
              class="text-slate-500 font-mono text-[10px] md:text-sm tracking-widest text-center px-1 md:px-2"
              >VIDEO FEED</span
            >
            <!-- Eye Tracking Node -->
            <div
              class="eye-tracker-horizontal absolute w-3 h-3 md:w-4 md:h-4 bg-[#F68C24] rounded-full shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(246,140,36,0.8)] z-20"
            >
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Saccade Success Divider Line -->
          <div
            class="w-px h-24 md:h-32 border-l-2 border-dashed border-[#F68C24]/50 absolute top-1/2 left-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 z-0"
          >
          </div>

          <div
            class="absolute bottom-6 md:bottom-8 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 bg-[#F68C24]/10 border border-[#F68C24]/30 text-[#F68C24] px-3 py-1.5 md:px-4 md:py-2 rounded text-[10px] md:text-xs font-mono text-center whitespace-nowrap z-10"
          >
            CLEAN HORIZONTAL FIELD
          </div>

          <!-- Mock Data Feed -->
          <div
            class="w-1/2 h-40 md:h-full md:max-h-[300px] bg-slate-800 rounded-lg border border-slate-700 flex items-center justify-center relative"
          >
            <span
              class="text-slate-500 font-mono text-[10px] md:text-sm tracking-widest text-center px-1 md:px-2"
              >LVA DATA PANEL</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Custom CSS for the Eye-Tracking Animations -->
  <style>
    /* Diagonal tracking from center face to top-right chart */
    .eye-tracker-diagonal {
      animation: scanDiagonal 3s ease-in-out infinite;
    }
    @keyframes scanDiagonal {
      0%,
      100% {
        top: 50%;
        left: 50%;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
      }
      20%,
      30% {
        top: 15%;
        left: 85%;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
      } /* Jumps to top right overlay */
      50%,
      60% {
        top: 50%;
        left: 50%;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
      } /* Jumps back to face */
      80%,
      90% {
        top: 15%;
        left: 85%;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
      }
    }

    /* Clean horizontal tracking locked for all screens */
    .eye-tracker-horizontal {
      animation: scanHorizontal 3s ease-in-out infinite;
    }
    @keyframes scanHorizontal {
      0%,
      100% {
        right: 10%;
        transform: translateY(0);
      }
      20%,
      30% {
        right: -110%;
        transform: translateY(0);
      } /* Glances right at data */
      50%,
      60% {
        right: 10%;
        transform: translateY(0);
      } /* Glances back to video */
      80%,
      90% {
        right: -110%;
        transform: translateY(0);
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Toggle Logic -->
  <script>
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
      const btns = document.querySelectorAll(".arch-btn");
      const viewProblem = document.getElementById("view-problem");
      const viewSolution = document.getElementById("view-solution");
      const title = document.getElementById("architecture-title");
      const desc = document.getElementById("architecture-desc");

      const contentMap = {
        problem: {
          title: "The Problem: Floating Overlays",
          desc: "Forces complex diagonal eye travel and creates visual interference. The moving video behind the chart creates a constant figure-ground conflict for the brain.",
          titleColor: "var(--text)",
        },
        solution: {
          title: "The Solution: Horizontal Sync",
          desc: "By extracting the data and locking it perfectly adjacent to the video, both streams remain within a clean horizontal foveal field. Visual occlusion is eliminated.",
          titleColor: "#F68C24",
        },
      };

      btns.forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
          const target = e.target.getAttribute("data-toggle");

          // 1. Update Button Styles
          btns.forEach((b) => {
            b.classList.remove("bg-[#F68C24]", "text-white", "shadow-md");
            b.classList.add("text-slate-400");
            b.classList.remove("active");
          });
          e.target.classList.remove("text-slate-400");
          e.target.classList.add(
            "bg-[#F68C24]",
            "text-white",
            "shadow-md",
            "active",
          );

          // 2. Update Text Context
          title.innerText = contentMap[target].title;
          title.style.color = contentMap[target].titleColor;
          desc.innerText = contentMap[target].desc;

          // 3. Swap Visuals
          if (target === "problem") {
            viewSolution.style.opacity = "0";
            viewSolution.style.pointerEvents = "none";

            viewProblem.style.opacity = "1";
            viewProblem.style.pointerEvents = "auto";
          } else {
            viewProblem.style.opacity = "0";
            viewProblem.style.pointerEvents = "none";

            viewSolution.style.opacity = "1";
            viewSolution.style.pointerEvents = "auto";
          }
        });
      });
    });
  </script>

  <Heading3
    isContentFirst={true}
    title="1. Synchronous Interface Architecture"
    subtitle="I designed a specialized split-view desktop layout that paired the video player directly with an adjacent data visualization panel. The goal was to ensure that the emotional telemetry (graphs, timelines, and confidence scores) mapped perfectly to the audio-visual timeline, allowing researchers to contextualize the data in real-time."
  >
    <div slot="media-slot" class="col-span-1 md:col-span-6 rounded-lg">
      <img src="../../projects/nemesysco/wireframe-1.webp" alt="" />
    </div>
  </Heading3>

  <!-- <ContentWithMedia
    imageFirst={false}
    imageCellWidth={8}
    contentCellWidth={4}
    contentImage="../../projects/nemesysco/wireframe-1.webp"
    contentTitle="The Idea"
    contentDescription=`TEST DESCRIPTION`
  /> -->

  <Heading3
    isContentFirst={false}
    title=`2. Diagnosing & Overcoming "Cognitive Tunneling"`
  >
    <div slot="media-slot" class="col-span-1 md:col-span-6 rounded-lg">
      <ImageLightbox
        src="../../projects/nemesysco/heatmap_2.webp"
        alt="Nemesysco UI Heatmap"
      />
    </div>

    <ul>
      <li class="max-w-[70ch] text-[var(--text)]/90 mb-2">
        <strong>The Insight:</strong> User testing revealed analysts fixated so heavily
        on the video that they suffered from inattentional blindness, completely missing
        critical data panel updates.Threshold-triggered micro-interactions
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[70ch] text-[var(--text)]/90 mb-2">
        <strong>The Solution </strong> Kept the UI "quiet" during baseline states,
        but engineered threshold-triggered micro-interactions.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[70ch] text-[var(--text)]/90 mb-2">
        <strong>Attention Hooks:</strong> When the AI hit a ≥89% confidence score,
        the UI deployed high-contrast color shifts and intentional motion to pull
        the user's eyes to the data exactly when it mattered.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Heading3>

  <!-- <SplitGallery /> -->
  <SplitGalleryLottie />

  <Heading3
    className={`pb-0!`}
    isContentFirst={true}
    centerText={true}
    title="3. Event-Driven Timeline Navigation"
    subtitle="Because deep-tech analysis requires heavy retrospective review, I designed an intelligent playback timeline. Whenever the system detected a significant shift in the subject's mood, the UI automatically plotted an interactive visual marker directly onto the video scrubber. This allowed users to instantly navigate the subject's emotional journey and jump directly to key milestones, rather than manually scrubbing through hours of raw footage."
  >
    <div slot="media-slot" class="w-full col-span-6">
      <div
        class="flex flex-col w-full max-w-[800px] mx-auto mt-12 gap-6 font-sans"
      >
        <div
          class="bg-[#01112B] rounded-lg overflow-y-auto max-h-[220px] flex flex-col custom-scrollbar shadow-xl md:min-h-[300px] min-h-[350px]"
        >
          <button
            id="list-item-1"
            popovertarget="popover-1"
            class="flex items-center gap-6 w-full px-6 py-4 hover:bg-[#152033] transition-all border-l-4 border-transparent cursor-pointer"
          >
            <div class="h-7 w-2 bg-[#f68c24]"></div>
            <div class="font-bold text-white text-lg w-12 text-left">0:11</div>
            <div class="text-slate-300 text-left text-[17px]">
              Subject is quite <strong class="font-bold text-white"
                >EMOTIONAL</strong
              > about this
            </div>
          </button>

          <button
            id="list-item-2"
            popovertarget="popover-2"
            class="flex items-center gap-6 w-full px-6 py-4 hover:bg-[#152033] transition-all border-l-4 border-transparent cursor-pointer"
          >
            <div class="h-7 w-2 bg-[#f68c24]"></div>
            <div class="font-bold text-white text-lg w-12 text-left">0:18</div>
            <div class="text-slate-300 text-left text-[17px]">
              Subject seems to be mostly <strong class="font-bold text-white"
                >ENERGETIC</strong
              >
            </div>
          </button>

          <button
            id="list-item-3"
            popovertarget="popover-3"
            class="flex items-center gap-6 w-full px-6 py-4 hover:bg-[#152033] transition-all border-l-4 border-transparent cursor-pointer"
          >
            <div class="h-7 w-2 bg-[#f68c24]"></div>
            <div class="font-bold text-white text-lg w-12 text-left">0:29</div>
            <div class="text-slate-300 text-left text-[17px]">
              Low levels of <strong class="font-bold text-white">STRESS</strong>
            </div>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
